# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# Modified Jacoby 2NT (Larry Cohen, "Modified Jacoby 2NT", larryco.com):
# responder's 2NT is the same game-forcing raise (jacoby-2nt.bid), but
# opener's rebids sort the hand by strength first and shape second, and
# responder relays for more:
#
#   4M   the worst minimum: 5-3-3-2, nothing extra
#   3♣   any other minimum              3♦ asks: 3♥ short, 3♠ 5-4-2-2,
#                                       3NT 6+ trumps, 4M 5-3-3-2, 4x a side suit
#   3♦   non-minimum, a singleton or void      3♥ asks which
#   3♥   non-minimum, 5-4-2-2                  3♠ asks for the four-card suit
#   3♠   non-minimum, 6+ trumps, no shortness
#   3NT  non-minimum, 5-3-3-2
#   4x   a good five-card side suit
#
# The suits are fixed: over 1♥ too, 3♥ is the 5-4-2-2 and 3♠ the six
# trumps (Cohen writes one schedule for both majors). Minimum is 14 HCP or
# fewer, the standard module's line. See modified-jacoby-2nt.notes.md.

module modified-jacoby-2nt "Modified Jacoby 2NT"
  kind   convention
  card   major_openings.jacoby_2nt.modified
  needs  jacoby-2nt
  skill  bidding_conventions/modified_jacoby_2nt
  param  rkcb  = slam.rkcb.play default false
  param  bw    = slam.blackwood.play default false
  param  cue = slam.cue_bids.play default false

# ── Opener's rebid ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
after 1M (P) 2N (P)
  4M  "Minimum, 5-3-3-2, nothing extra"
      shows hcp<=12, shape 5-3-3-2, M=5
      priority 1                       # ahead of 3♣, which these hands also fit
  3C  "Minimum, 14 HCP or less: 3♦ asks"  alert
      shows hcp<=14
      artificial
  3D  "15+, a singleton or void: 3♥ asks where"  alert
      shows hcp>=15, shortest<=1
      artificial
  3H  "15+, 5-4-2-2: 3♠ asks for the four-card suit"  alert
      shows hcp>=15, shape 5-4-2-2, M=5
      artificial
  3S  "15+, six or more trumps, no singleton or void"  alert
      shows hcp>=15, M>=6, shortest>=2
      artificial
  3N  "15+, 5-3-3-2"
      shows hcp>=15, shape 5-3-3-2, M=5
  4x  "15+, a good five-card side suit"
      shows hcp>=15, x>=5, quality(x)>=good
      when  x is not M, M is S | x is not S

# ── They bid over the 2NT ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cohen: double shows shortness in their suit, a new suit is natural or
# a control, 3NT a balanced maximum with the ace or king of their suit,
# the jump to 4M a dead minimum with 6-3-2-2, and pass a flat hand. The pass is forcing (Rick, 2026-10-28): we are in a game
# force, so responder must act, by doubling them for penalty or bidding
# on. It is marked artificial because the engine otherwise drops a pass
# below game in a game force.
after 1M (P) 2N (2x) | 1M (P) 2N (3x) when x is not M
  X   "Short in {x}: a singleton or void"  alert
      shows x<=1
      artificial
      priority 16                      # ahead of everything else here, as the shortness is the news
  3N  "15+, balanced, the ace or king of {x}"
      shows hcp>=15, balanced, has(A,x) | has(K,x)
      priority 15
  4M  "Dead minimum, 6-3-2-2"
      shows hcp<=12, shape 6-3-2-2, M=6
      priority 15
  3y  "Natural or a control in {y}"
      shows (y>=5, quality(y)>=good) | has(A,y) | has(K,y)
      when  y is not M, y is not x
      priority 15
  4y  "Natural or a control in {y}"
      shows (y>=5, quality(y)>=good) | has(A,y) | has(K,y)
      when  y is not M, y is not x, M is S | y is not S
      priority 15
  P   "Forcing pass: a flat hand"  alert
      artificial
      priority 14                      # below the descriptions, above the generic competitive calls

# Responder after the forcing pass (Cohen: "after which, responder's
# X = penalty"; Rick, 2026-10-28): opener is flat, perhaps an awful
# 5-3-3-2, so with their suit held responder doubles them, whatever his
# strength. Else game; with slam interest the slam modules act.
after 1M (P) 2N (2x) P (P) | 1M (P) 2N (3x) P (P) when x is not M
  X   "Penalty: {x} held"
      shows x>=4 | (x>=3, has(A,x) | has(K,x))
      priority 15
  4M  "Game: no slam interest"
      shows !slam_interest(M)
      priority 14

# ── They double or bid over an ask ───────────────────────────────────
# Cohen: "If they double Asks or re-asks: XX = business, Pass = S1, etc.
# If they bid after Ask or re-ask: X = Penalty, Pass = S1, etc." Pass is
# the first step and the bids follow in order from the cheapest
# (`step(1)` the second step). The pass is artificial, so the game force
# keeps it legal and makes responder bid again. 2NT is the first ask:
# over their double of it the steps hold; over their bid, the schedule
# above (X short there, as Cohen says).

define mj_business(a) = a>=4, has(A,a) | has(K,a)

after 1M (P) 2N (X)
  XX  "Business: 15+, balanced, to play 2NT redoubled"
      shows hcp>=15, balanced
      priority 16
  P   "Step 1: a minimum, 14 or less"  alert
      shows hcp<=14
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(1)  "Step 2: 15+, a singleton or void"  alert
      shows hcp>=15, shortest<=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(2)  "Step 3: 15+, 5-4-2-2"  alert
      shows hcp>=15, shape 5-4-2-2, M=5
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(3)  "Step 4: 15+, six or more trumps, no singleton or void"  alert
      shows hcp>=15, M>=6, shortest>=2
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(4)  "Step 5: 15+, 5-3-3-2"  alert
      shows hcp>=15, shape 5-3-3-2, M=5
      artificial
      priority 15

# The 3♦ ask after a minimum.
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (X)
  XX  "Business: good diamonds"
      shows mj_business(D)
      priority 16
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (3z) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (4z)
  X   "Penalty: good {z}"
      shows mj_business(z)
      priority 16
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (*) when !rho.last=P
  P   "Step 1: a singleton or void"  alert
      shows shortest<=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(1)  "Step 2: 5-4-2-2"  alert
      shows shape 5-4-2-2, M=5
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(2)  "Step 3: six or more trumps, no singleton or void"  alert
      shows M>=6, shortest>=2
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(3)  "Step 4: 5-3-3-2"  alert
      shows shape 5-3-3-2, M=5
      artificial
      priority 15

# The 3♥ ask after shortness.
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (X)
  XX  "Business: good hearts"
      shows mj_business(H)
      when  M is S
      priority 16
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (3z) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (4z)
  X   "Penalty: good {z}"
      shows mj_business(z)
      priority 16
after 1S (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (*) when !rho.last=P
  P   "Step 1: a void"  alert
      shows C=0 | D=0 | H=0
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(1)  "Step 2: a singleton club"  alert
      shows C=1, D>=1, H>=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(2)  "Step 3: a singleton diamond"  alert
      shows D=1, C>=2, H>=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(3)  "Step 4: a singleton heart"  alert
      shows H=1, C>=2, D>=2
      artificial
      priority 15
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (*) when !rho.last=P
  P   "Step 1: a void"  alert
      shows C=0 | D=0 | S=0
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(1)  "Step 2: a singleton club"  alert
      shows C=1, D>=1, S>=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(2)  "Step 3: a singleton diamond"  alert
      shows D=1, C>=2, S>=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  step(3)  "Step 4: a singleton spade"  alert
      shows S=1, C>=2, D>=2
      artificial
      priority 15

# The 3♠ ask after 5-4-2-2.
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3H (P) 3S (X)
  XX  "Business: good spades"
      shows mj_business(S)
      when  M is H
      priority 16
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3H (P) 3S (3z) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3H (P) 3S (4z)
  X   "Penalty: good {z}"
      shows mj_business(z)
      priority 16
after 1S (P) 2N (P) 3H (P) 3S (*) when !rho.last=P
  P        "Step 1: four clubs"     alert  shows C=4  artificial  priority 15
  step(1)  "Step 2: four diamonds"  alert  shows D=4  artificial  priority 15
  step(2)  "Step 3: four hearts"    alert  shows H=4  artificial  priority 15
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3H (P) 3S (*) when !rho.last=P
  P        "Step 1: four clubs"     alert  shows C=4  artificial  priority 15
  step(1)  "Step 2: four diamonds"  alert  shows D=4  artificial  priority 15
  step(2)  "Step 3: four spades"    alert  shows S=4  artificial  priority 15

# The 3NT re-ask: where is the void?
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (4z)
  X   "Penalty: good {z}"
      shows mj_business(z)
      priority 16
after 1S (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (*) when !rho.last=P
  P        "Step 1: club void"     alert  shows C=0  artificial  priority 15
  step(1)  "Step 2: diamond void"  alert  shows D=0  artificial  priority 15
  step(2)  "Step 3: heart void"    alert  shows H=0  artificial  priority 15
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (*) when !rho.last=P
  P        "Step 1: club void"     alert  shows C=0  artificial  priority 15
  step(1)  "Step 2: diamond void"  alert  shows D=0  artificial  priority 15
  step(2)  "Step 3: spade void"    alert  shows S=0  artificial  priority 15

# ── Responder: the relays ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Over the minimum (Rick, 2026-11-07): "modified jacoby 2nt is mostly
# useful because responder can jump to game with no slam interest,
# after a 3C rebid by opener. the main advantage is that it doesn't
# give the defenders any clues to opener's distribution. so we don't
# want to always ask. but with say 15+ HCP, responder should probably
# ask." So 3♦ with 15+ HCP, else 4M at once. This overrides the
# double-dummy measurement, which cannot see what the relays tell the
# defenders (notes, "Ask over 3♣ only with 15+").
#
# Over the non-minimum answers (3♦ short, the void) the relays stay
# wide: responder relays whenever slam is possible with everything
# working, his support points and opener's top HCP 27 or more
# (`mj_relay_floor`). Cohen: "If responder still has slam interest, he
# can ask further".
define mj_relay_floor = 27
define mj_try(t) = slam_interest(t) | tp(t) + partner.hcp.max >= mj_relay_floor

after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P)
  3D  "Asks opener to describe the minimum"  alert
      shows hcp >= 15
      sets  ask=mj_relay
      artificial
      priority 15                      # the relay, ahead of the control bids (12-14)
  4M  "Game: no slam interest opposite a minimum"
      shows hcp <= 14
      priority 15                      # Rick 2026-11-07: tell the defenders nothing

after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P)
  3H  "Asks where the singleton or void is"  alert
      shows mj_try(M)
      sets  ask=mj_relay
      artificial
      priority 15

after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3H (P)
  3S  "Asks for opener's four-card side suit"  alert
      shows slam_interest(M)
      sets  ask=mj_relay
      artificial
      priority 15

# ── Opener answers the 3♦ ask (a minimum) ────────────────────────────
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P)
  3H  "Minimum, a singleton or void"  alert
      shows shortest<=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  3S  "Minimum, 5-4-2-2"  alert
      shows shape 5-4-2-2, M=5
      artificial
      priority 15
  3N  "Minimum, six or more trumps, no singleton or void"  alert
      shows M>=6, shortest>=2
      artificial
      priority 15
  4M  "Minimum, 5-3-3-2"
      shows shape 5-3-3-2, M=5
      priority 15
  4x  "Minimum, a good five-card side suit"
      shows x>=5, quality(x)>=good, shortest>=1
      when  x is not M, M is S | x is not S
      priority 16                      # ahead of a singleton most such hands also hold; a void goes first (3♥)

# The next step asks again (Cohen: "After opener's 3♥ or 3♠ answer to
# 3♦, next step asks, using same schedule"), one step up from the
# non-minimum schedule: over 3♥ (short), 3♠ asks: 3NT a void (4♣ asks
# where: 4♦ clubs, 4♥ diamonds, 4♠ the other major), 4♣/4♦/4♥ a
# singleton club, diamond, other major. Over 3♠ (5-4-2-2), 3NT asks:
# 4♣ clubs, 4♦ diamonds, 4♥ the other major. Over 1♥ the singleton or
# four spades lands on 4♥, the spade void on 4♠: past game, and
# responder still has 4NT.
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P)
  3S  "Asks where the singleton or void is"  alert
      shows mj_try(M)
      sets  ask=mj_relay
      artificial
      priority 15
# Responder does not make the 3NT ask himself: nothing below reads the
# four-card suit, and relaying cost 53 IMPs on 34 boards against going
# on at once (notes). Opener still answers a partner who asks.
after 1S (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P)
  3N  "A void: 4♣ asks where"  alert   shows C=0 | D=0 | H=0     artificial  priority 15
  4C  "A singleton club"  alert        shows C=1, D>=1, H>=1     artificial  priority 15
  4D  "A singleton diamond"  alert     shows D=1, C>=2, H>=1     artificial  priority 15
  4H  "A singleton heart"  alert       shows H=1, C>=2, D>=2     artificial  priority 15
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P)
  3N  "A void: 4♣ asks where"  alert   shows C=0 | D=0 | S=0     artificial  priority 15
  4C  "A singleton club"  alert        shows C=1, D>=1, S>=1     artificial  priority 15
  4D  "A singleton diamond"  alert     shows D=1, C>=2, S>=1     artificial  priority 15
  4H  "A singleton spade"  alert       shows S=1, C>=2, D>=2     artificial  priority 15
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P)
  4C  "Asks where the void is"  alert
      sets  ask=mj_relay
      artificial
      priority 15
after 1S (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P) 4C (P)
  4D  "Club void"  alert       shows C=0  artificial  priority 15
  4H  "Diamond void"  alert    shows D=0  artificial  priority 15
  4S  "Heart void"  alert      shows H=0  artificial  priority 15
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P) 4C (P)
  4D  "Club void"  alert       shows C=0  artificial  priority 15
  4H  "Diamond void"  alert    shows D=0  artificial  priority 15
  4S  "Spade void"  alert      shows S=0  artificial  priority 15
after 1S (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3S (P) 3N (P)
  4C  "Four clubs"  alert      shows C=4  artificial  priority 15
  4D  "Four diamonds"  alert   shows D=4  artificial  priority 15
  4H  "Four hearts"  alert     shows H=4  artificial  priority 15
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3S (P) 3N (P)
  4C  "Four clubs"  alert      shows C=4  artificial  priority 15
  4D  "Four diamonds"  alert   shows D=4  artificial  priority 15
  4H  "Four spades"  alert     shows S=4  artificial  priority 15

# ── Opener answers the 3♥ ask (non-minimum, short somewhere) ─────────
# Steps: a void (3♠), then a singleton in clubs, diamonds, the other
# major. After the void, 3NT asks where: clubs, diamonds, the other major.
after 1S (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P)
  3S  "A void: 3NT asks where"  alert
      shows C=0 | D=0 | H=0
      artificial
      priority 15
  3N  "A singleton club"  alert
      shows C=1, D>=1, H>=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  4C  "A singleton diamond"  alert
      shows D=1, C>=2, H>=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  4D  "A singleton heart"  alert
      shows H=1, C>=2, D>=2
      artificial
      priority 15
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P)
  3S  "A void: 3NT asks where"  alert
      shows C=0 | D=0 | S=0
      artificial
      priority 15
  3N  "A singleton club"  alert
      shows C=1, D>=1, S>=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  4C  "A singleton diamond"  alert
      shows D=1, C>=2, S>=1
      artificial
      priority 15
  4D  "A singleton spade"  alert
      shows S=1, C>=2, D>=2
      artificial
      priority 15

after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P)
  3N  "Asks where the void is"  alert
      shows mj_try(M)
      sets  ask=mj_relay
      artificial
      priority 15
after 1S (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P)
  4C  "Club void"  alert       shows C=0  artificial  priority 15
  4D  "Diamond void"  alert    shows D=0  artificial  priority 15
  4H  "Heart void"  alert      shows H=0  artificial  priority 15
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P)
  4C  "Club void"  alert       shows C=0  artificial  priority 15
  4D  "Diamond void"  alert    shows D=0  artificial  priority 15
  4H  "Spade void"  alert      shows S=0  artificial  priority 15

# ── Opener answers the 3♠ ask (non-minimum, 5-4-2-2) ─────────────────
after 1S (P) 2N (P) 3H (P) 3S (P)
  3N  "Four clubs"  alert      shows C=4  artificial  priority 15
  4C  "Four diamonds"  alert   shows D=4  artificial  priority 15
  4D  "Four hearts"  alert     shows H=4  artificial  priority 15
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3H (P) 3S (P)
  3N  "Four clubs"  alert      shows C=4  artificial  priority 15
  4C  "Four diamonds"  alert   shows D=4  artificial  priority 15
  4D  "Four spades"  alert     shows S=4  artificial  priority 15

# ── Responder: keycard once the relays have placed opener's shape ────
# (Rick, 2026-11-06, bridge-classroom #83/#84: "ask about south shape
# and learn of spade void then try keycard"; 2026-11-07: "keycard
# should be the stronger hand. the idea of the relays is it will allow
# us to find low HCP slams when there is a good fit.") Once a relay
# answer has placed opener's singleton or void (`shown_short`),
# responder counts his working values (slam-entry.bid, `working_count`:
# support points less the honours wasted opposite the shortness, plus
# opener's floor; `working_slam`, 26). With that, slam: the stronger hand
# by what has been shown (`stronger_hand`: responder's HCP at least
# opener's floor; always opposite a minimum) asks for keycards; the
# weaker, opposite a non-minimum, bids the cheapest suit below game
# ("my values work: you ask") and opener asks. Where there is no room
# below game responder asks himself. Or 14 HCP with an honour in
# opener's good five-card side suit (the 4x answer). Less is left to
# the slam modules (game, mostly). Not after the 5-4-2-2's four-card
# suit: that branch lost 223 IMPs on 46 boards (notes). The keycard
# answers and the placement are rkcb-1430.bid's (blackwood.bid's
# without RKCB). The asks are `mj_relay`, not `relay`: minor-
# transfers.bid's `when answered relay` (pass with clubs) read our
# relays and passed a 4♥ answer.
define mj_slam(t) = working_slam(t)
define mj_side_fits(x) = x is not trump, partner.x >= 5, has(A,x) | has(K,x) | has(Q,x), hcp >= 16
define mj_room = (trump is not C, under_game(C)) | (trump is not D, under_game(D)) | (trump is not H, under_game(H)) | (trump is not S, under_game(S))
define mj_fits = (mj_slam(trump), stronger_hand | !mj_room) | mj_side_fits(C) | mj_side_fits(D) | mj_side_fits(H) | mj_side_fits(S)

when answered mj_relay, we.trump is H | we.trump is S, we.forcing = game
  4N  "Keycard ask in {trump}: opener's shape fits"
      when  rkcb
      shows mj_fits
      sets  ask=keycards(trump)
      artificial
      priority 14
  4N  "Blackwood: opener's shape fits"
      when  bw, !rkcb
      shows mj_fits
      sets  ask=aces
      artificial
      priority 14
  cheapest(C)  "Slam values opposite your shape: you ask"  alert
      shows mj_slam(trump), !stronger_hand
      when  rkcb | bw, trump is not C, under_game(C), shown_short   # public: read only where it can be the signal
      sets  ask=mj_captain
      artificial
      prefer 0 - cheapest_rank(C)
      priority 14
  cheapest(D)  "Slam values opposite your shape: you ask"  alert
      shows mj_slam(trump), !stronger_hand
      when  rkcb | bw, trump is not D, under_game(D), shown_short   # public: read only where it can be the signal
      sets  ask=mj_captain
      artificial
      prefer 0 - cheapest_rank(D)
      priority 14
  cheapest(H)  "Slam values opposite your shape: you ask"  alert
      shows mj_slam(trump), !stronger_hand
      when  rkcb | bw, trump is not H, under_game(H), shown_short   # public: read only where it can be the signal
      sets  ask=mj_captain
      artificial
      prefer 0 - cheapest_rank(H)
      priority 14
  cheapest(S)  "Slam values opposite your shape: you ask"  alert
      shows mj_slam(trump), !stronger_hand
      when  rkcb | bw, trump is not S, under_game(S), shown_short   # public: read only where it can be the signal
      sets  ask=mj_captain
      artificial
      prefer 0 - cheapest_rank(S)
      priority 14

# Opener, the stronger hand, asks over responder's "you ask".
when asked mj_captain, we.trump is H | we.trump is S
  4N  "Keycard ask in {trump}: the stronger hand asks"
      when  rkcb
      sets  ask=keycards(trump)
      artificial
      priority 15
  4N  "Blackwood: the stronger hand asks"
      when  bw, !rkcb
      sets  ask=aces
      artificial
      priority 15

# With a side suit open, the asker bids a control instead of asking
# (Rick, 2026-11-10, Bridge-Classroom report: 1H 2N 3D 3H 3NT 4C 4S with
# AK.QJ8653.JT97.A). Past game it is first-round, and only 4♠ over
# hearts: a control above 4NT would take the keycard ask away (five-level
# ones cost 13-26 IMPs on the Jacoby scenarios). A suit skipped is
# denied, so partner goes on only if he covers it. A new suit here has
# no natural meaning, so these do not wait for `slam.cue_bids.play`.
when asked mj_captain, we.trump is H | we.trump is S
  cheapest(C)  "Control bid in ♣"  alert
      when  trump is not C, under_game(C)
      when  side_suit_uncontrolled, controlled(C)
      sets  ask=control(C), ladder=control
      artificial
      prefer 0 - cheapest_rank(C)
      priority 16
  cheapest(D)  "Control bid in ♦"  alert
      when  trump is not D, under_game(D)
      when  side_suit_uncontrolled, controlled(D)
      sets  ask=control(D), ladder=control
      artificial
      prefer 0 - cheapest_rank(D)
      priority 16
  cheapest(H)  "Control bid in ♥"  alert
      when  trump is not H, under_game(H)
      when  side_suit_uncontrolled, controlled(H)
      sets  ask=control(H), ladder=control
      artificial
      prefer 0 - cheapest_rank(H)
      priority 16
  cheapest(S)  "Control bid in ♠"  alert
      when  trump is not S, under_game(S)
      when  side_suit_uncontrolled, controlled(S)
      sets  ask=control(S), ladder=control
      artificial
      prefer 0 - cheapest_rank(S)
      priority 16
  cheapest(S)  "Control bid in ♠: first-round control"  alert
      when  trump is H, !under_game(S), !kb_spade_ask
      when  side_suit_uncontrolled, first_round(S)
      sets  ask=control(S), ladder=control
      artificial
      prefer 0 - cheapest_rank(S)
      priority 16

# Past game, without the suit partner skipped: back to five of the
# trump suit (control-bids.bid has this when the card plays them).
when asked control(t), !cue, we.trump is H, partner.last = 4S
  5{trump}  "No slam: a suit is open"
      priority -6

# Over 1♥ the spade void is shown with 4♠, past game: without the
# values for keycard, back to five hearts.
after 1H (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P) 4C (P) 4S (P)
  5H  "No slam: back to hearts"
      priority 13

# ── Opener after responder declines (Rick, 2026-11-07) ───────────────
# "normally opener doesn't continue for slam exploration after
# responder chooses not to try, unless opener has 19+ points." When
# responder bids 4M over any of opener's answers or relay answers,
# opener passes with 18 points or fewer; with 19+ the slam modules
# decide as before. Above the keycard ask and the control bids.
after 1M (P) 2N (P) 3x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3N (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 4x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3N (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 4x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P) 4x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 4x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3N (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 4x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 4x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3H (P) 3S (P) 3N (P) 4C (P) 4x (P) 4M (P) | 1M (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) 3D (P) 3S (P) 3N (P) 4x (P) 4M (P)
  P   "Responder declined: no slam without 19+"
      shows points <= 18
      priority 16
